  "worked_solution": "To compute ${f}^{\u2032}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u={x}^{2}$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{0}^{u}t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[0,u],$ and so by FTC II we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\sqrt{u} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})\\cdot u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\sqrt{u} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\sqrt{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
